@startuml
actor Student
participant Browser
participant "Flask Route" as Route
participant "Flask-Login\nAuthorization" as Auth
participant Database as DB
participant "Test / Scoring Service" as Service
participant "Recommendation Service" as Recommendations
participant "Result Page" as Result

Student -> Browser: Select published test
Browser -> Route: POST /mock-tests/{id}/start
Route -> Auth: require authenticated user
Auth --> Route: user identity / access decision
Route -> DB: load published test and in-progress attempt
DB --> Route: test metadata and question links
Route -> DB: create TestAttempt(started_at, in_progress)
DB --> Route: attempt id
Route --> Browser: redirect to active test
Browser -> Route: GET active test page
Route -> DB: load question text and options
DB --> Route: questions (answer keys available server-side)
Route --> Browser: render question data only
note over Browser,Route
  The active response excludes correct answers
  and explanations.
end note

Student -> Browser: Select answers and submit
Browser -> Route: POST answers + elapsed-time hint
Route -> Auth: verify attempt owner or admin
Auth --> Route: authorized
Route -> DB: reload attempt, test links, answer keys
DB --> Route: scoring records
Route -> Service: grade submitted IDs and choices
Service -> Service: validate choices and calculate score
Service -> DB: persist AttemptAnswer and evaluated TestAttempt
DB --> Service: commit
Service -> Recommendations: refresh from stored performance
Recommendations -> DB: read performance and replace active recommendations
DB --> Recommendations: saved recommendations
Recommendations --> Service: recommendations refreshed
Service --> Route: score summary
Route --> Browser: redirect to result
Browser -> Result: GET result page
Result -> DB: load owned attempt, answers, and review data
DB --> Result: persisted result records
Result --> Browser: render score, review, and recommendations
@enduml
